        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "4c60b0f813438146e5485060e2e56a333a2c3558",
            "parents": [
                "4989fc36d6d60916aa06359aeda782abd65f9b42"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/30/84330/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                "username": "manojkiraneda"
            },
            "createdOn": 1760077312,
            "author": {
                "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                "username": "manojkiraneda"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/conf/machine/include/tpm1.inc",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks like this came from the facebook commits but why do we need a DISTRO_FEATURE? Isn't the MACHINE_FEATURE enough? If we do need it, why not call it \"tpm1\" to stay consistent with tpm2?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/conf/machine/include/tpm1.inc",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "\"tpm\" DISTRO_FEATURE is defined by the meta-tpm layer, and I am just trying to append it to machine configuration as needed. Usually distro features are version agnostic, However, TPM support in the yocto is an exception to this rule because TPM 1.2 and TPM 2.0 are fundamentally incompatible software stacks, with non-overlapping utilities and APIs and having both \u201ctpm\u201d(supports tpm 1.2) and \u201ctpm2\u201d(supports tpm2) DISTRO_FEATURES helps manage this mess cleanly.\n\nThe way I understood this was that we use MACHINE_FEATURES - to indicate that a board has TPM1.X hardware or TPM2.X hardware & we use DISTRO_FEATURES - to indicate that this distro has TPM software capabilities & support in general , so both are needed in this case as software stack & utilities are not common both of hardware."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-core/packagegroups/packagegroup-openbmc-tpm.bb",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please move to recipes-phosphor rather than recipes-core."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-core/packagegroups/packagegroup-openbmc-tpm.bb",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-core/packagegroups/packagegroup-openbmc-tpm.bb",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "GPL-2.0?\n\nWe shouldn't need a LICENSE directive for a package group, because it doesn't have any code, but GPL-2.0 on what is just a recipe file definitely isn't what should be here.  Apache-2.0 or leave it blank."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-core/packagegroups/packagegroup-openbmc-tpm.bb",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "> GPL-2.0?\n> \n> We shouldn't need a LICENSE directive for a package group, because it doesn't have any code but GPL-2.0 on what is just a recipe file definitely isn't what should be here. Apache-2.0 or leave it blank.\n\nsure, I have removed it like other package groups in the meta-phosphor layer."
                }
            ],
